THE CLOJURE NAMESPACE SOURCE -- ONE SOURCE, NAMED
================================================================================
Author: Muhammad Ishaq Khan (clojure lane).
Target: src/ast/real-clojure-analyzer.ts  (THE LANE's OWN WRITE SCOPE).
Apply: git apply this file, then read the landed text back.

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS -- THE PRICE IS A FUNCTION OF THE NAMESPACE SOURCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MEASURED, on the same tree, the same population (646 files / 3 repos), the farm
corpus root, the same 43,324-edge population, the same join rule:

  841  the join's reach under the PRODUCTION's per-file namespace
       (`clojureFileNamespace`, src/ast/project-index.ts:1563)
  853  the join's reach under the analyzer's PER-SYMBOL `scope`
  854  the join's reach in the INDEX's key space
  856  the join's reach under the PATCH's OWN namespace source -- the analyzer's
       `(ns ...)` module symbol's name -- WHICH IS WHAT THE LANDED JOIN USES
  994  what the GATE actually moved (the gate's own counter)

THE SAME RULE, PRICED FOUR WAYS, SPREADING 15 ROWS PER SOURCE. The gate moved
994, which is not any of the four. THE PRICE IS NOT A PROPERTY OF THE LANGUAGE
ALONE; IT IS A PROPERTY OF (the analyzer's namespace source) x (the gate's key
space). A CELL's JOIN PRICE NAMES ITS NAMESPACE SOURCE, and a price is not
comparable with another lane's price until both name theirs.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
It makes the ANALYZER publish ONE namespace source, and it makes that source the
PRODUCTION's own rule:

  1. `let fileNamespace = ""` -- the FILE's namespace, a separate value from the
     RUNNING `currentNamespace` (which `in-ns` moves mid-file).
  2. `fileNamespace` is captured ONCE, at the FIRST `ns` form, and never moves.
  3. The MODULE SYMBOL is published for the `ns` form ONLY, and carries
     `fileNamespace` -- not `currentNamespace`.

WHY THE `in-ns` MODULE SYMBOL STOPS BEING PUBLISHED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The production's `clojureFileNamespace` matches the `ns` form ONLY. A file whose
only namespace form is `in-ns` has NO file namespace. The landed gate's own
comment already states the rule it wants: "A file that declares no namespace at
all has NO entry here, and the join then answers nothing for it." Before this
patch the analyzer published `user` for the 44 files with no namespace form and
published the `in-ns` namespace for the 17 `in-ns` files -- so the gate's
`nsByFile` held a namespace the production does not have. THAT IS THE SOURCE
MISMATCH, and it is worth 15 rows on the price.

CONSEQUENCE TO BE MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This patch CHANGES THE ANALYZER's PUBLICATION. The price after it MUST BE
RE-MEASURED (the gate's arm, the same population, the same root) -- the lane
does not state a new price from this patch, because a price stated from a patch
is a price with no instrument behind it. The lane's expectation is that the
gate's namespace source and the production's per-file namespace become the SAME
SOURCE, and that the 15-row source difference CLOSES. Whether it closes, and by
how much, is the measurement.

The `in-ns` namespace EFFECT on symbol scope is UNCHANGED: `currentNamespace`
still moves on `in-ns`, so the symbols' `scope` and ownership are as they are
today (CLJ-D31). Only the MODULE SYMBOL's publication changes.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES NOT TOUCH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * `script/m14/incoming-gate.ts` and `script/m14/incoming-rule.ts` -- the Lead's
    files, untouched.
  * `src/ast/project-index.ts` -- the production's `clojureFileNamespace` is
    ALREADY EXPORTED and is the source this patch makes the analyzer agree with.
    No edit there is needed for the namespaces to be one source.
  * The 13-row analyzer publication gap -- UNFIXED, as ruled.

